  "description": "Full PACE ECDH-GM AES-128 session authenticated with a CAN rather than the MRZ. The MSE:Set AT carries DO83 = 02 (CAN_PACE_KEY_REFERENCE) and DO84 (parameterId 13); K_pi derives from the ISO/IEC 8859-1 octets of the CAN with no hash (P11 §9.7.3 Table 14), where the MRZ path hashes. runners:[\"dart\"]; upstream ships the CAN reference constant but never sets it, so its createPaceKey cannot derive this key at all. No published CAN chain exists (App G/H/I are all MRZ), so the wire here is sim-synthesized from the App G.1 ECDH-GM material with the password swapped; K_pi itself is pinned independently by the python-oracle rows in kdf_pace.json. Domain, both keypairs and the nonce are App G.1's, so a diff against pace_session_ecdh_gm_aes128.json isolates exactly what the password changes. The final step is the first post-PACE protected command.",
